il' service or 'redis_latency' for 'valkey-cart'.\n\nSo, the next tool to use would be 'get_metrics' with a query targeting the 'email' service's latency or the 'valkey-cart' Redis metrics. That would help identify if there's a performance issue in those services causing the long durations observed in the traces.\n</think>\n\nget_metrics  \nThe traces for the **checkout** service show a long duration in the `send_email` span (6.5 seconds) and a feature flag evaluation that bypassed a cart operation. To investigate potential performance bottlenecks or errors in the **email** service or **valkey-cart** (Redis), I will query real-time metrics for HTTP latency and Redis latency using Prometheus. This will help identify if the email service is slow or if Redis is experiencing high latency, which could explain the observed delays.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=1042, prompt_tokens=10487, total_tokens=11529, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe5f-adc7-74a1-a34d-e764d6e8228e-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10487, 'output_tokens': 1042, 'total_tokens': 11529}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='9c428813-4aa0-4743-84b8-32d95326da01')]]
