Alternatively, they could check the Redis pod's configuration to ensure it's properly set up to expose metrics, but since the previous query for Redis also didn't return data, maybe the Redis instance isn't configured to expose metrics either.\n\nBut since the user is focusing on the email service's metrics issue, the next logical step is to check the email service's deployment or service manifest to see if there's a metrics endpoint. They could use kubectl to describe the deployment or service and look for any annotations or ports related to metrics. Alternatively, they might need to check the application's code or configuration to see if it's supposed to expose metrics on a specific path and port. If the email service isn't instrumented, that could be the root cause of the missing metrics, which in turn might be related to the long duration observed in the send_email span. If the email service isn't properly monitored, it could be causing delays or errors that aren't being captured in the traces, leading to the observed issues.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe -n astronomy-shop deployment email"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b5a373accaa816cc', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 505, 'prompt_tokens': 12233, 'total_tokens': 12738, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfe60-960e-7f40-99d3-71237fd9505d-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe -n astronomy-shop deployment email'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b5a373accaa816cc', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12233, 'output_tokens': 505, 'total_tokens': 